<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 203 0 R
/E (MODA WEEK INTERNATIONAL was developed from a vision to create an independent fashion enterprise capable of connecting distinctive talent, brands, and creative professionals with broader markets through professionally produced experiences. Since its inception, MWINTL has grown across borders, bringing together emerging and established designers, models, artists, entrepreneurs, media, sponsors, and industry leaders. Its productions encompass runway presentations, exhibitions, networking, brand activations, cultural showcases, and strategic collaborations that provide participants with visibility, valuable connections, and pathways toward new opportunities. At the heart of MWINTL is a commitment to using fashion as a powerful bridge between commerce, creativity, and culture. Through its events, the company welcomes diverse voices and works to uplift communities internationally by highlighting local talent, honoring cultural identity, encouraging economic participation, and creating access to broader audiences. Each destination contributes its own character to the MWINTL experience, allowing regional creativity to enter a global conversation while fostering meaningful relationships among businesses, creators, and audiences. This approach transforms each production into more than a runway presentation it becomes a meeting point for discovery, exchange, representation, and growth. Guided by an entrepreneurial philosophy of adaptability, innovation, and continuous development, MWINTL continues to strengthen its presence within fashion, media, hospitality, entertainment, and related sectors. What began as a vision is becoming an interconnected commercial platform built to open doors across borders, cultivate lasting partnerships, elevate communities, and shape a meaningful international legacy through fashion.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
